+# The P2MR rescue verifier: the Rust crate voleith, vendored
+
+The verifier of the P2MR rescue lane ([doc/p2mr-rescue.md](../../doc/p2mr-rescue.md)): the crate
+`voleith` of ark0-rescue, which implements the VOLE-in-the-head proofs of its `SPEC.md` v0.2
+revision 2 (version byte `0x02`, statement `0x01`), and the crates it depends on. CMake builds it into
+a static library that holds the verifier and its C ABI only (`CMakeLists.txt`, here).
+
+## Source
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| repository | ark0-rescue, as kept on branch `main` of `duncan0k/workbench` (private) |
+| commit | `f5a2bc0c9a6b40684a9975c3435ff332ba5a5050`, "rust: the fixture name without basename; narrow two descriptions" (2026-10-24), the reviewed crate; it contains `ff4ea00`, vendored before |
+| directory | `rust/`, git tree `833d94e8fa20d46e4d1780ba2a18f64e95f707e5` |
+| here | `voleith/`, all 53 files of that tree, unmodified |
+| protocol | `SPEC.md` v0.2 revision 2 of the same commit; the vectors and the three implementations (Python, Rust, Go) of that repository agree on it |
+
+The crate has the cargo feature `prover`, on by default, which the node's build turns off
+(`--no-default-features`): no prover code is compiled into the library. The crate's own
+`check-verifier-only.sh` shows how to check this with `nm`.
+
+From `ff4ea00` (vendored first) to `f5a2bc0`, what the verifier computes is unchanged. Its SHAKE256
+is now in `src/sym.rs`, built on the Keccak-f[1600] permutation of the `keccak` crate, in place of
+the `sha3` crate. The library depends only on `keccak` and `zeroize`; `sha3` stays a dev-dependency,
+the reference for that sponge's test. The rest of the range is the command-line tools, their tests,
+and the build checks (`build-windows.sh`, `check-verifier-only.sh`, `check-windows-shadowing.sh`,
+`windows/`, `tests/fixtures/`).
+
+## Dependencies
+
+`vendor/` is what `cargo vendor --locked --versioned-dirs` writes for `voleith/Cargo.lock` with
+Rust 1.97.0, with one change: the packages that no build of this tree compiles keep only their
+`Cargo.toml` and a `.cargo-checksum.json` listing just that file (the package checksum, which
+`Cargo.lock` pins, is unchanged). Where the manifest names no path for the library (packages
+published by older versions of cargo: `block-buffer`, `digest`, `generic-array`), cargo needs
+`src/lib.rs` to parse it, and that file is kept and listed too. Cargo reads their manifests to resolve the lock file and compiles
+none of them. They are the dev-dependencies of the crate's tests and benchmarks (`sha3`, `serde_json`,
+`secp256k1` and theirs) and the target-specific dependencies of `getrandom` on other systems. The
+full `cargo vendor` output is 46 packages, 2,505 files; this is 7.8 MB in 637 files (with `ff4ea00`,
+13 packages whole and 754 files). To regenerate it:
+
+```
+cd voleith && CARGO_HOME=$(mktemp -d) cargo +1.97.0 vendor --locked --versioned-dirs ../vendor-new
+python3 ../stub-vendor.py ../vendor-new cfg-if,cpufeatures,getrandom,keccak,libc,zeroize
+diff -r ../vendor-new ../vendor        # no output
+```
+
+On 2026-10-24, for `f5a2bc0`, this gave `vendor/` itself.
+
+Compiled, and kept whole:
+
+| package | licence | compiled into |
+|---|---|---|
+| `cfg-if-1.0.5` | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | the test-only tools only (getrandom) |
+| `cpufeatures-0.2.17` | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | the library on aarch64 (keccak) |
+| `getrandom-0.3.4` | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | the test-only tools only (feature `cli`) |
+| `keccak-0.1.6` | Apache-2.0 OR MIT | the library |
+| `libc-0.2.190` | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | the library on aarch64 Linux and macOS (cpufeatures); the test-only tools (getrandom) |
+| `zeroize-1.8.2` | Apache-2.0 OR MIT | the library |
+
+Manifest only, never compiled:
