+
+`voleith` itself states no licence in its `Cargo.toml` and the ark0-rescue repository has no licence
+file at that commit: it is the project's own code (duncan0k), used here under the MIT licence of this
+tree. Every vendored package that is compiled may be used under MIT.
+
+The one vendored file with CR bytes is `generic-array`'s `src/lib.rs` (CRLF line endings), which
+`git am` would turn into LF. `.gitattributes` keeps that package binary, so `format-patch` carries it
+byte for byte. No file of `voleith/` has a CR byte.
+
+## Build
+
+`CMakeLists.txt` runs, from `voleith/`, through `cargo-build.cmake`:
+
+```
+cargo build --release --offline --locked --frozen --no-default-features --lib --target <triple>
+```
+
+Isolation and pinning:
+
+- **Toolchain.** The toolchain of `rust-toolchain.toml` (Rust 1.97.0). At configure time its own
+  `rustc` and `cargo` are found in its sysroot (`rustc --print sysroot`), not rustup's proxies, and
+  both are checked to be 1.97.0. The build runs those two binaries, with `RUSTC` naming that `rustc`.
+- **Environment.** Every `CARGO_*`, `RUST*` (`RUSTC_WRAPPER`, `RUSTFLAGS`, `RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN`, ...)
+  and make job server variable, and `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH`, is removed.
+- **Configuration files.** `CARGO_HOME` is a new, empty directory in the build tree. The build
+  stops if a `.cargo/config.toml` or `.cargo/config` is in any parent of the crate or the build
+  directory.
+- **Profile.** The crate's release profile (`opt-level = 3`, `lto = true`, `codegen-units = 1`,
+  `panic = "unwind"`, which the C ABI needs to catch a panic) is given again with `--config`, where
+  it overrides anything else. The build fails if cargo's verbose log shows any crate compiled with
+  `panic=abort`.
+- **Flags and sources.** `vendor/` replaces crates.io. `CARGO_ENCODED_RUSTFLAGS` holds only
+  `--remap-path-prefix` for this directory and the build directory, and `-Cdebuginfo=0`.
+- **Rebuilds.** Every file of `voleith/` and `vendor/` is a dependency (`CONFIGURE_DEPENDS`). A change
+  to any of them removes the cargo target directory and builds the library again from nothing:
+  cargo takes vendored packages to be immutable and would otherwise keep objects of a vendored file
+  that has changed.
+
+The archive is imported as the target `voleith` and linked into `bitcoin_consensus` and
+`bitcoinkernel`. A shared `bitcoinkernel` exports none of its symbols: it is linked with
+`--exclude-libs` on ELF platforms and `-hidden-l` on macOS. A DLL exports only what is
+`__declspec(dllexport)`. A static `bitcoinkernel` does not hold the archive's objects, so the archive
+is installed next to it as `libbitcoinkernel_voleith.a`; `libbitcoinkernel.pc` lists it, with the
+system libraries it needs, in `Libs.private` (`pkg-config --static`). Of the system libraries
+`--print native-static-libs` names on Linux (`-lgcc_s -lutil -lrt -lpthread -lm -ldl -lc`), `-lgcc_s`
+and `-lutil` are not passed: nothing in the archive needs libutil, and `_Unwind_*` comes from the C++
+link (libgcc_s, or libgcc_eh with `-static-libgcc`).
+
+With `-DBUILD_TESTS=ON`, a second build of the same crate with `--features cli --bins` makes the
+crate's command-line tools, `voleith-prove` and `voleith-verify`, for the functional tests, which
+prove rescue spends as they run. They are not linked into anything and not installed.
+
